id: pm-gh1609
title: "GH-1609: recover killed commit owners and bound lock waits with a monotonic clock"
description: "New GitHub report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1609 compares Linux Node24.19.0 plain non-Git tracker behavior: a strace-injected SIGKILL at the first rename, followed by another writer, reportedly succeeds4/4 on2026.10.21 but fails3/4 on2026.10.26 with lock_conflict and owner process dead after roughly3seconds. The report dates the change to2026.10.23 commit fencing and describes a separate frozen-clock downstream timeout. Reproduce independently and compare the owner-death reclaim and commit-fence cleanup gates, preserving live/unknown owner and stale-writer safety. Do not infer a root cause or bypass fences from the report alone."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T03:16:18.150Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T11:21:03.385Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#1326c2a1b31ee2f18421aa9e"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce the real-wall-clock SIGKILL sequence in disposable non-Git trackers on the reported old and current versions; If confirmed fix preserves mutation fencing and audit history with negative controls for live and unknown owners; Separate monotonic acquisition deadlines from owner liveness and verify Node and Bun public SDK behavior
parent: pm-02z97f
risk: high
confidence: high
expected_result: "A provably dead writer is recovered safely after an interrupted commit, and bounded acquisition does not hang under a frozen wall clock; live or ambiguous ownership retains protection."
